From 029e734cc7f5d52077927b7c9cfc227052586159 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 20:33:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] patch 2: agent-side DPP-over-TCP relay in the BWL/HAL
 layer

Add the HAL plumbing that lets hostapd relay DPP frames to/from the agent
over a local TCP socket (127.0.0.1:8908):

- slave_wlan_hal.h: new Event::Dpp_* values and init_dpp_relay()/
  stop_dpp_relay()/dpp_send_frame()/is_dpp_client_connected() virtuals.
- dpp_relay_socket.{h,cpp} (new): platform-agnostic raw-socket engine for
  the relay listener, driven by the owning HAL backend's event loop.
- nl80211 backend: wires dpp_relay_socket into slave_wlan_hal_nl80211's
  fd-based event loop; ap_wlan_hal_nl80211 writes dpp_controller /
  dpp_configurator_connectivity into hostapd config for DPP-AKM VAPs.
- whm backend: mirrors the same behavior via ambiorix WiFi.DPP. object
  events instead of a raw socket.
- ap_manager.cpp: handles Event::DPP_CREDENTIALS_READY, writing wireless
  extender credentials from wpa_supplicant to tmpfs for son_slave_thread.

Signed-off-by: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
